From 4abc8c1d807c5d1766357bb08f1bb51502c72ccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:26:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The client's own tests and guards keep up with the series

The client-tests run found 16 tests failing on the pinned benilla with the series applied. Each
one is either a guard that counts what the series adds, a test written against an older state of
the code, or a real gap.

Real gaps:
- `SetMissileLook`'s own speed was read from the tenth argument; the add-on and the doc's
  signature put it ninth (0040).
- The new look's cloud layer (`LookSkyMaterial`) had no warm rig, so its first sight was a live
  pipeline compile (0068).
- Six systems that name `SelfPlayer` ran before the Net stage that tags it (0003, 0004, 0031),
  `dress_missiles` wrote transforms the lanes' drain also writes (0030), and four systems of
  `OnExit(InWorld)` ran outside the session's end order (0003, 0027, 0054, 0059).
- The three systems that learn of a new UI VM now read `ui_script::VmGeneration`, so only the
  feed layer names the VM (the wall's count was 44 against 42).

Guards that count what the series adds, updated with the reason: the 50 globals past 1.12 (the
add-on's seams, grouped by patch), the world API wall (the new look is published, 39 other items
filed as leaks), the four look passes the warm pass exempts, the surface golden of the VM parity
test, and the actionable-pair ceiling of the `Update` schedule.

Stale tests: the afterimage's deepened tint (0027), the water grain's default (0085), and the
torn-down unit's build, which needs `PreviewTint` (0017).
